;
; passenger-side-plate.ngc - mill the passenger's side fixture plate.
;
; Copyright (C) 2026 narrativecollapse.  Free software under the WTFPL,
; version 2, with no warranty: see LICENSE.
;
; The plate is described in chapter 14 of "Machining the AR15 Lower
; Receiver Forging" by Ray Brandes.  Run passenger-side-chamfer.ngc on it
; afterwards, once its 10 degree edge is cut (plate-angle.ngc).
;
; Stock: 6.000 x 2.500 x 0.500 aluminium, faced (facemill-plate.ngc), in
; the vise with at least 0.313 above the jaws.
;
; Datums: X0 Y0 at the plate's top right corner, so it runs to X-6.000
; Y-2.500.  Z0 on its top surface.
;
; The high part of the plate is X-2.750 to X0; the thinned area is the
; rest.  The three slots are cut in an order that lets each one plunge
; where an earlier one has already cleared.
;


; -- settings ---------------------------------------------------------

#<clear_z> = 0.100

#<tool> = 3             ; 0.375 end mill
#<tool_dia> = 0.375
#<rpm> = 2000
#<feed> = 5

#<stepover> = [#<tool_dia> / 2]
#<step_down> = [#<tool_dia> / 2]
#<finish> = 0.010

#<thin_z> = -0.106
#<slot_z> = -0.313


; -- program ----------------------------------------------------------

o<ar15-start> call [#<clear_z>]
o<ar15-tool> call [#<tool>] [#<rpm>] [#<feed>] [#<tool_dia>]

; The thinned area: the left end to X-2.750, the whole width.  It plunges
; off the top edge; the finishing pass climb-mills the X-2.750 wall.
o<ar15-pocket> call [-6.000 - #<tool_dia> / 2] [#<tool_dia> * 1.5] [-2.750] [-2.500 - #<tool_dia> * 1.5] [0] [#<thin_z>] [#<tool_dia>] [#<stepover>] [#<step_down>] [#<finish>]

; The top slot: along the top edge from the left end to X-2.500, 0.500
; deep (Y), so it runs 0.250 into the high part.  It plunges off the top
; edge.
o<ar15-pocket> call [-6.000 - #<tool_dia> / 2] [#<tool_dia> + 0.010] [-2.500] [-0.500] [0] [#<slot_z>] [#<tool_dia>] [#<stepover>] [#<step_down>] [#<finish>]

; The upright slot: X-3.875 to X-3.375, from the top edge down to
; Y-1.750.  It plunges inside the top slot.
o<ar15-pocket> call [-3.875] [0] [-3.375] [-1.750] [#<thin_z>] [#<slot_z>] [#<tool_dia>] [#<stepover>] [#<step_down>] [#<finish>]

; The lower slot: Y-1.000 to Y-1.500, from the upright slot to X-2.500,
; so it too runs 0.250 into the high part.  Its start wall is a cutter
; diameter inside the upright slot, so it plunges there.
o<ar15-pocket> call [-3.375 - #<tool_dia> - 0.010] [-1.000] [-2.500] [-1.500] [0] [#<slot_z>] [#<tool_dia>] [#<stepover>] [#<step_down>] [#<finish>]

o<ar15-end> call
m2
